[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/284894981","html_url":"https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/14997#issuecomment-284894981","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/14997","id":284894981,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4NDg5NDk4MQ==","user":{"login":"ghetolay","id":1864528,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NjQ1Mjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1864528?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay","html_url":"https://github.com/ghetolay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghetolay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-03-07T23:29:03Z","updated_at":"2017-03-07T23:29:03Z","body":"I've just look at the `DefaultKeyValueDiffer` code and it's scary :). \r\nI'm assuming this is because it handles deep mutable object. This made me think, Angular don't want to force users to use immutable data and this is fine but this adds complexity when it comes to handle things like differs (ngFor, ngStyle, ngClass...).\r\n\r\nWould not it be worth it to have multiple implementation for immutable and mutable data so those using immutable data (cause of OnPush, NgRx etc...) could benefit from lightweight implementation ?\r\n\r\nI'm saying all that because I'm assuming `DefaultKeyValueDiffer` is so complex because of mutable data so I hope I'm not wrong here.","author_